# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Tested against the real build, not written from a template: the policy below
# was checked by serving dist/ with these exact headers and loading every screen
# in a browser with the console treated as fatal. It is as tight as it is
# because this app loads NOTHING from anywhere else — no CDN, no font host, no
# analytics, no cloud TTS. Every script, style, font and JSON file is our own.
#
# If a future change needs a new origin, widen this deliberately and say why.
# A CSP relaxed in a hurry is a CSP nobody trusts afterwards.
#
# ── Two things to know before changing anything here ───────────────────────
#
# HSTS carries `preload`, and that directive is a COMMITMENT rather than a
# setting. On its own it does nothing: the domain has to be submitted to
# hstspreload.org, and it has NOT been, and must not be without Shahin saying
# so. Once submitted, `includeSubDomains` forces HTTPS on every future
# subdomain of frenchmavie.com, and removal from the list takes months and
# travels with browser releases. The directive is here deliberately, so that
# submitting stays a decision rather than becoming a prerequisite — but
# submitting is a separate, later decision and is not implied by this line.
#
# There is NO CSP reporting, so a violation in a learner's browser is invisible
# to us. That is a known blind spot and a deliberate one: `report-uri` needs an
# endpoint, an endpoint that is not ours would send a learner's address and the
# page they were on to a third party, and that breaks the rule this whole file
# exists to keep. We accept being blind rather than accept that. If reporting
# ever matters enough, it has to be our own endpoint on our own origin.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; media-src 'self'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), ambient-light-sensor=(), autoplay=(), battery=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), document-domain=(), encrypted-media=(), fullscreen=(self), gamepad=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), hid=(), idle-detection=(), local-fonts=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), picture-in-picture=(), publickey-credentials-get=(), screen-wake-lock=(), serial=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# Hashed assets are immutable: the filename changes when the content does.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The service worker and the shell must never be served stale, or a learner
# keeps an old app after a deploy.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
